# gocha API — requests for the VS Code REST Client extension
# (humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request" above any ### block.
# JetBrains IDEs run this file too, but their client does not do the
# {{login.response...}} capture — paste the token into @token there.
#
# Start here: run "Log in as admin" (or "Register"), and every request
# below picks the token up automatically.

@host = http://localhost:8080

# Dev accounts created with:
#   gochactrl register --email admin@example.com --password admin12345 --role admin
#   gochactrl register --email cli-user@example.com --password secret123
@adminEmail = admin@example.com
@adminPassword = admin12345
@userEmail = cli-user@example.com
@userPassword = secret123


### Healthcheck — no auth
GET {{host}}/healthcheck


### Register a new account (always role "user"; 409 if the email is taken)
# display_name is optional (max 64 chars) — omit it for a nameless account
# @name register
POST {{host}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new-userexample.com",
  "password": "secret123",
  "display_name": "New User"
}

### Log in as admin — most requests below need this one
# @name login
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### Log in as a plain user — the non-admin in the 403 checks below
# @name loginUser
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

### Log in as the account registered above — the outsider in the group chat
# @name loginOutsider
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "new-user@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}


# The access token is the only credential the API takes. It is also set as
# an HttpOnly access_token cookie, so a browser needs no header at all.
@token = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}
@userToken = {{loginUser.response.body.$.access_token}}
@userId = {{loginUser.response.body.$.id}}
@outsiderToken = {{loginOutsider.response.body.$.access_token}}


### Who am I
GET {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### No token → 401
GET {{host}}/me

### Cookie instead of the header (what a browser does)
GET {{host}}/me
Cookie: access_token={{token}}


## User directory (any signed-in user)

### Who you can add to a chat — id, email, display_name only.
# Excludes you and the system account, so every entry is a valid participant.
GET {{host}}/users/directory?limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


## Users (admin only)

### List users, oldest first
GET {{host}}/users?limit=20&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List as a plain user → 403 (missing users:read)
GET {{host}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Update a user — any subset of email/role/password
# Changing the password revokes every token issued to that user so far.
PATCH {{host}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "user",
  "display_name": "Renamed User"
}

### Soft-delete a user (deleted_at; the Ethora mirror is kept)
DELETE {{host}}/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Restore a soft-deleted user (409 if they are not deleted)
POST {{host}}/users/{{userId}}/restore
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


## Chats

### Create a public chat — open to any authenticated user
# @name publicChat
POST {{host}}/chats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Town square",
  "type": "public"
}

### Create a group chat — readable only by its participants
# Needs at least 2 of them; the creator is always added, so listing
# yourself is optional. Here that is the admin plus {{userId}}.
# @name groupChat
POST {{host}}/chats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Standup",
  "type": "group",
  "participants": ["{{userId}}"]
}

@publicChatId = {{publicChat.response.body.$.id}}
@groupChatId = {{groupChat.response.body.$.id}}

### Add participants to an existing chat
# Creator or admin only — a plain participant gets 403. Ids already in the
# chat are skipped, so replaying this request is harmless.
POST {{host}}/chats/{{groupChatId}}/participants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participants": ["{{userId}}"]
}

### Same call as a non-creator → 403
POST {{host}}/chats/{{groupChatId}}/participants
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participants": ["{{userId}}"]
}

### Send a message (text: 1-2000 chars)
POST {{host}}/chats/{{publicChatId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Hello from api.rest"
}

### List messages, newest first (limit 1-100, default 50)
GET {{host}}/chats/{{publicChatId}}/messages?limit=50&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A participant reads the group chat → 200
GET {{host}}/chats/{{groupChatId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Someone outside the group reads it → 403
GET {{host}}/chats/{{groupChatId}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{outsiderToken}}

### Delete a chat (admin only)
DELETE {{host}}/chats/{{publicChatId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
